# Unit01
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 基础词Unit01核心词汇

abandon/əˈbændən/放弃；抛弃/He abandoned his plan to travel abroad.
ability/əˈbɪləti/能力；才能/She has the ability to solve complex problems.
able/ˈeɪbl/有能力的；能干的/He is able to finish the task on time.
abnormal/æbˈnɔːrml/不正常的；异常的/The abnormal weather has affected crops.
aboard/əˈbɔːrd/在船（车、飞机）上/We went aboard the ship at noon.
abolish/əˈbɑːlɪʃ/废除；废止/The government decided to abolish the old law.
about/əˈbaʊt/关于；大约/The meeting is about education reform.
above/əˈbʌv/在…上面/The temperature is above average today.
abroad/əˈbrɔːd/在国外/She studied abroad for three years.
absence/ˈæbsəns/缺席；不在/His absence from the meeting was noticed.
absent/ˈæbsənt/缺席的；不在的/He was absent from class yesterday.
absolute/ˈæbsəluːt/绝对的；完全的/I have absolute confidence in you.
absorb/əbˈzɔːrb/吸收；吸引/Plants absorb water through their roots.
abstract/ˈæbstrækt/抽象的/Abstract art is not easy to understand.
absurd/əbˈsɜːrd/荒谬的；可笑的/That is an absurd excuse.
abundance/əˈbʌndəns/丰富；充裕/There is an abundance of natural resources.
abundant/əˈbʌndənt/丰富的；充裕的/The area has abundant rainfall.
abuse/əˈbjuːs/滥用；虐待/Drug abuse is a serious social problem.
academic/ˌækəˈdemɪk/学术的；学院的/He published an academic paper last year.
accelerate/əkˈseləreɪt/加速；促进/The car accelerated quickly on the highway.
accept/əkˈsept/接受；承认/She accepted the job offer gladly.
access/ˈækses/进入；通道/Students have access to the library 24 hours a day.
accident/ˈæksɪdənt/事故；意外/The traffic accident caused a long jam.
accommodate/əˈkɑːmədeɪt/容纳；提供住宿/The hotel can accommodate 500 guests.
accompany/əˈkʌmpəni/陪伴；伴随/He accompanied her to the hospital.
accomplish/əˈkɑːmplɪʃ/完成；实现/She accomplished her goal ahead of time.
account/əˈkaʊnt/账户；描述/Please open a bank account for me.
accumulate/əˈkjuːmjəleɪt/积累；堆积/He accumulated a lot of experience over the years.
accurate/ˈækjərət/准确的；精确的/The report is accurate and detailed.
accuse/əˈkjuːz/指控；谴责/He was accused of stealing the money.
achieve/əˈtʃiːv/达到；取得/She achieved great success in her career.
acknowledge/əkˈnɑːlɪdʒ/承认；感谢/He acknowledged his mistake publicly.
acquaint/əˈkweɪnt/使熟悉；使了解/Let me acquaint you with the new rules.
acquire/əˈkwaɪər/获得；学到/She acquired a new skill through practice.
across/əˈkrɔːs/穿过；在对面/The bridge across the river is very long.
act/ækt/行动；法案/We must act quickly to solve the problem.
actual/ˈæktʃuəl/实际的；真实的/The actual cost was higher than expected.
adapt/əˈdæpt/适应；改编/She adapted to the new environment quickly.
add/æd/增加；补充/Please add some sugar to the coffee.
addict/əˈdɪkt/使上瘾/He is addicted to playing video games.
address/əˈdres/地址；演讲/The president delivered an address to the nation.
adequate/ˈædɪkwət/足够的；适当的/The supply is adequate for our needs.
adjust/əˈdʒʌst/调整；适应/Please adjust the volume of the TV.
administer/ədˈmɪnɪstər/管理；执行/The nurse administered the medicine to the patient.
admire/ədˈmaɪər/钦佩；欣赏/I admire her courage and determination.
admit/ədˈmɪt/承认；允许进入/He admitted that he had made a mistake.
adopt/əˈdɑːpt/采纳；收养/They decided to adopt a child.
advance/ədˈvæns/前进；进步/Technology continues to advance rapidly.
advantage/ədˈvæntɪdʒ/优势；有利条件/Her experience gives her an advantage.
